 "section_summary": "This section contains pages 2 to 55 of an official postwar statistical roster of educational institutions in Hiroshima Prefecture, covering Ministry of Education, prefectural, municipal, and town or village schools. The institutions surveyed include higher schools, normal schools, colleges, vocational schools, middle schools, girls' high schools, special schools for the blind and deaf-mute, youth schools, elementary schools, and kindergartens. Each school entry details administrative classification, location, founding date, and comparative gender-disaggregated statistics for students and faculty as of April 30, 1946, and November 30, 1946. Pages 298 to 300 are duplicate impressions of preceding pages 295 to 297 within the document bundle.",
